# Independently authored PG two-phase commit (2PC)
# sentinel slice for the GPL MTR-format runner. NOT
# copied or adapted from MySQL's mysql-test/.
#
# Existing coverage (do NOT duplicate):
#   - PREPARE TRANSACTION / COMMIT PREPARED / ROLLBACK
#     PREPARED: ZERO prior coverage.
#
# Pre-existing rejection shape patterns:
#   - "Expected: AS, found: <X>" — pre-existing at
#     prepare_basic_extra (MySQL PREPARE p FROM '...'
#     form rejection). Same fingerprint applies here
#     because sqlparser's PREPARE parser expects
#     `PREPARE name AS stmt` and treats TRANSACTION
#     as an identifier-position name token.
#   - "Expected: end of statement, found: <KW>" —
#     pre-existing (RESET TIME ZONE / RESET SESSION
#     AUTHORIZATION at PR #399, many others).
#
# This slice pins:
#
#   PREPARE TRANSACTION 'gid' (2 forms) — "Expected:
#   AS, found: '<gid>'" at col 21:
#     - sqlparser parses `PREPARE TRANSACTION` as
#       `PREPARE name=TRANSACTION` and then expects
#       `AS stmt`, gets the gid string-literal,
#       errors. PG 2PC PREPARE TRANSACTION cannot
#       be expressed in zeta.
#
#   COMMIT PREPARED 'gid' (2 forms) — "Expected: end
#   of statement, found: PREPARED" at col 8:
#     - sqlparser parses COMMIT as a complete
#       statement; the trailing PREPARED is
#       unexpected.
#
#   ROLLBACK PREPARED 'gid' (2 forms) — "Expected:
#   end of statement, found: PREPARED" at col 10:
#     - Same shape as COMMIT PREPARED, different
#       column (ROLLBACK is 2 chars longer than COMMIT).
#
# Big-picture finding:
#
#   PG two-phase commit (2PC, X/Open XA-style
#   external coordinator) is entirely unreachable.
#   All three PG 2PC statements parse-reject. Apps
#   porting PG distributed transaction managers that
#   use 2PC must rewrite to:
#     - Saga pattern (compensating transactions in
#       application logic)
#     - Single-database transactions with retry
#     - Whatever distributed-txn primitives zeta
#       exposes (per project README, distributed
#       work is feature-gated)
#
# Adaptation notes:
#   # zeta-adapt: KNOWN GAP — PG 2PC family (PREPARE
#     TRANSACTION / COMMIT PREPARED / ROLLBACK
#     PREPARED) all parse-reject at sqlparser. No
#     direct substitute for X/Open XA-style 2PC.
#     Use Saga compensating-txn pattern app-side.

--echo === PREPARE TRANSACTION 'gid' (2 forms) → "Expected: AS, found: '<gid>'" at col 21 ===

# sqlparser's PREPARE arm parses `TRANSACTION` as the
# prepared-statement name; then expects `AS stmt`,
# gets the gid string-literal, errors.
--error 1064
PREPARE TRANSACTION 'gid_1';
--error 1064
PREPARE TRANSACTION 'app/tx/42';

--echo === COMMIT PREPARED 'gid' (2 forms) → "Expected: end of statement, found: PREPARED" at col 8 ===

--error 1064
COMMIT PREPARED 'gid_1';
--error 1064
COMMIT PREPARED 'app/tx/42';

--echo === ROLLBACK PREPARED 'gid' (2 forms) → "Expected: end of statement, found: PREPARED" at col 10 ===

# Same shape as COMMIT PREPARED, col 10 vs col 8
# (ROLLBACK is 2 chars longer than COMMIT).
--error 1064
ROLLBACK PREPARED 'gid_1';
--error 1064
ROLLBACK PREPARED 'app/tx/42';
